  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 1250 AM CST Sun Nov 8 2026\n\nTaking a look at the synoptic patterns heading into the work\nweek, northwesterly flow aloft looks to continue over us, with \nan upper level low pushing into the Southern Plains southwest \nof the forecast area. This upper level energy looks to \ncontinue sliding south of us on Tuesday, with guidance \ncontinuing to keep any rain chances away from us. We may not be\nable to stay completely away from precipitation chances however,\nas another system pushes in from the northwest by Wednesday,\nincreasing rain chances to 30-40% (slightly higher than \nprevious forecasts). This is still a low-confidence scenario, as\nensemble discrepancies still exist, so we'll just keep \nmonitoring it for now. \n\nOtherwise, temperatures will climb into the 60s and 70s through\nmidweek before cooler air filters in from the north by late week.",
